  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "IronBee (ironbee.ai) is an AI QA engineer: it verifies code changes against the running app and keeps the evidence. It is not related to the IronBee open-source web application firewall.",
      "The console is at https://console.ironbee.ai.",
      "Install the CLI with `npm install -g @ironbee-ai/cli`, sign in with `ironbee login`, and set up a project with `ironbee install`.",
      "In GitHub workflows, use the action as `ironbee-ai/ironbee-action@v1` and pass the `IRONBEE_API_KEY` secret as the `ironbee_api_key` input.",
      "In GitLab pipelines, include the component `gitlab.com/ironbee-ai/ironbee-gitlab/verify@v1`; it reads the `IRONBEE_API_KEY` CI/CD variable by default.",
      "In Bitbucket Pipelines, run the pipe `docker://ghcr.io/ironbee-ai/ironbee-bitbucket:v1` and pass `IRONBEE_API_KEY: $IRONBEE_API_KEY` and `BITBUCKET_OAUTH_TOKEN: $BITBUCKET_OAUTH_TOKEN` under its `variables:`.",
      "Console scenarios (https://docs.ironbee.ai/console/scenarios) and CLI saved scenarios (https://docs.ironbee.ai/cli/guides/scenarios) are separate features.",
      "For plans and prices, link to https://ironbee.ai/pricing; the website is the source of truth for them."
    ]
  },
